# Command markless

## What does this command do:

A terminal markdown viewer with image support

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && curl -sSfL https://github.com/jvanderberg/markless/releases/download/v0.9.29/markless-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | tar -xz -C ~/.local/bin markless && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/markless`
For Raspberry Pi install using: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && curl -sSfL https://github.com/jvanderberg/markless/releases/download/v0.9.29/markless-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | tar -xz -C ~/.local/bin markless && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/markless`
For Mac install using: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && curl -sSfL https://github.com/jvanderberg/markless/releases/download/v0.9.29/markless-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz | tar -xz -C ~/.local/bin markless && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/markless`  (no Homebrew formula exists)
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && curl -sSfL https://github.com/jvanderberg/markless/releases/download/v0.9.29/markless-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | tar -xz -C ~/.local/bin markless && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/markless`

> Note: the Mac container runs Fedora Linux on ARM (aarch64), not x86_64. When a
> package is not installed via `dnf`, download the `aarch64`/`arm64` build of the
> binary — never the `x86_64`/`amd64` build used on the Fedora workstation.
> The container's `~/.local` is wiped on rebuild, so reinstall after a rebuild.

Alternative on any host with a Rust toolchain: `cargo install markless --locked`
The Linux builds need glibc 2.39 or newer.

## Command path

For Fedora run: `~/.local/bin/markless`
For Raspberry Pi run: `~/.local/bin/markless`
For Mac run: `~/.local/bin/markless`
For Mac container run: `~/.local/bin/markless`

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/jvanderberg/markless

## Command options

# View a markdown file
markless README.md

# Browse the current directory (default when no path is given)
markless .

# Browse a directory
markless src/

# Watch the file and auto-reload on change
markless -w <file.md>

# Hide / show the table of contents sidebar at start
markless --no-toc <file.md>
markless --toc <file.md>

# Disable inline images (placeholders only)
markless --no-images <file.md>

# Force an image protocol: kitty, sixel, iterm2, halfblock
markless --image-mode kitty <file.md>
markless --force-half-cell <file.md>

# Force the highlight theme background: auto, light, dark
markless --theme dark <file.md>

# Limit the word-wrap width
markless --wrap-width 100 <file.md>

# Use an external editor instead of the built-in one
markless --editor vim <file.md>
markless --no-editor <file.md>

# Render inline math as images instead of Unicode
markless --no-inline-math <file.md>
markless --inline-math <file.md>

# Save current flags as defaults / clear saved defaults
markless --theme dark --no-toc --save
markless --clear

# Debugging
markless --perf <file.md>
markless --render-debug-log /tmp/markless.log <file.md>

# Version / help
markless --version
markless --help

# Key bindings (in the viewer)
#   j/k or arrows  scroll          Space/b    page down/up
#   Ctrl-d/Ctrl-u  half page       g/G        top/bottom
#   /              search          Enter/Esc  next match / clear
#   t / T          toggle TOC / toggle and focus TOC
#   B / F          browse mode / file-only mode
#   e / Ctrl-e     edit mode       Ctrl-s     save
#   w              toggle watch    r/R        reload
#   o              open links 1-9  ?/F1       help
#   q / Ctrl-c     quit
